            <ArticleTitle>Headaches and neck pain in farmers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The prevalence of headache and neck pain in farmers was determined by use of a questionnaire. Information about activities which increased the symptoms and about the treatments sought was also recorded. Results showed that 77.7% of farmers experienced neck pain and 79.2% experienced headache. Driving a tractor was the activity which was most frequently described as increasing symptoms in both conditions. While driving a tractor, farmers are exposed to whole-body vibration and assume a rotated neck posture. The contribution of these factors to the development of headache and neck pain is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
